    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Minor scale",
      "body": "Play the white keys from A up to the next A. The notes are the same as C major, but starting on A, and it sounds darker. That is a **minor scale**.\n\n**Why it matters:** Sad songs, many film themes and lots of rock are in minor keys. Telling major from minor is one of the first things a band ear needs.",
